# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R3), the
# shape beside it: this module spells `holding.Holder`, so its unit reads
# `fixedbugs-563-holder.h`, after its own groups' headers and without the
# group `holding` writes above it, whose header defines the `Need` the first
# spells (design.md §4.1). `holding`'s own unit compiles. Until 2026-10-10 the
# refusal said *repair the header*; it says now which header the module
# writes above it and that the module spelling the record needs a group
# naming it.
use holding

function main()
    h = holding.make(v: 3)
    print(h.v)
